  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x+3 & =-2 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x & =-5 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}\u2061x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$\n\nThen, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(-\\frac{4}{5})\u2248-0.9273\n$$\n\nThis value is outside the required domain. To get a value inside the range, we add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=x+2\\pi =-0.9273+2\\pi \u22485.3559\n$$\n\nSo, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=5.3559.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.9273.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.9273.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041597/assets/d8951c588af989cc5a77b213f25a485b8a6e9db1d0f164fc326e65d40c0385c7.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.9273 \\\\  & \u22484.0689\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx\u22484.1,\\,x\u22485.4.\n$$",
